// Monetary reserves for settlement in money and reserves (`econ::payments::settle`,
// `game::Switches::payments_settle`, docs/state.pt-BR.md, "Padrão-ouro, reservas e balanço de
// pagamentos", slice 2). Read only with the switch on.
//
// Sources:
// - gold_1925: Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System, *Banking and Monetary
//   Statistics 1914–1941* (Washington, 1943), Table 160, "Gold reserves of central banks and
//   governments", pp. 544–551, row "1925—Dec.", in millions of dollars with gold at $20.67 per
//   fine ounce. Scanned on FRASER (Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis),
//   https://fraser.stlouisfed.org/title/banking-monetary-statistics-1914-1941-38 (file
//   BMS14-41_complete.pdf). A publication of the US government: public domain.
//   The table's colonies go to the market that holds them in the scenario: Algeria and Morocco
//   to France, Java (the Netherlands Indies) to the Netherlands. Countries with no figure for
//   December 1925 in the table start with no gold: China, Ecuador (from 1927), Guatemala
//   (from 1926), Danzig, Albania, Turkey, Siam, Persia and the Belgian Congo (from 1927).
//   Foreign exchange held by central banks is not in the table and starts at zero everywhere.
// - monetary_share: League of Nations, *Report of the Gold Delegation of the Financial
//   Committee* (Geneva, 1932), §121(a): "in the four years 1926 to 1929 somewhat more than $250
//   million of gold per annum were added to the visible monetary stocks ... rather less than
//   $150 million remained for non-monetary consumption", that is 250 of some 400 million a year
//   of new gold. Scanned by the National Library of Scotland,
//   https://deriv.nls.uk/dcn23/1903/6301/190363014.23.pdf. Public domain (League of Nations,
//   1932).
//
// The gold is valued at the catalogue's base price of the good `gold`: millions of dollars over
// `dollars_per_kg` ($20.67 an ounce × 32.1507 troy ounces in a kilogram) give the kilograms.
(
    dollars_per_kg: 664.556,
    // Per mille of each country's mine output that goes to its central bank.
    monetary_share: 625,
    gold_1925: [
        ("USA", 3985.4),
        ("FRA", 5.9), // Algeria
        ("ARG", 450.6),
        ("AUS", 162.5),
        ("AUT", 2.1),
        ("BEL", 52.9),
        ("BOL", 6.6),
        ("BRA", 54.3),
        ("RAJ", 108.6), // British India
        ("BUL", 8.0),
        ("CAN", 156.8),
        ("CHL", 34.0),
        ("COL", 14.6),
        ("CZE", 27.1),
        ("DEN", 56.1),
        ("EGY", 16.6),
        ("SAL", 5.4),
        ("EST", 1.3),
        ("FIN", 8.4),
        ("FRA", 711.0),
        ("GER", 287.8),
        ("GRE", 12.7),
        ("HUN", 10.4),
        ("ISL", 0.6),
        ("ITA", 221.6),
        ("JAP", 575.8),
        ("NLD", 73.4), // Java
        ("LAT", 4.5),
        ("LTU", 3.2),
        ("MEX", 16.7),
        ("FRA", 0.4), // Morocco
        ("NLD", 178.7),
        ("NZL", 37.7),
        ("NOR", 39.5),
        ("PER", 21.5),
        ("POL", 25.8),
        ("POR", 9.3),
        ("ROM", 48.5),
        ("SAF", 43.6),
        ("ESP", 489.5),
        ("SWE", 61.6),
        ("CHE", 90.5),
        ("GBR", 694.8),
        ("URY", 56.8),
        ("SOV", 93.9),
        ("VEN", 16.4),
        ("YUG", 14.7),
    ],
)
